WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:04.471
Area tells us how much flat space a shape covers.

00:04.921 --> 00:11.887
We measure area in square units. This rectangle is four squares long and three squares tall.

00:12.337 --> 00:16.725
Count the squares inside. There are three rows of four.

00:17.175 --> 00:24.406
That is twelve square units. Instead of counting every square, multiply the length by the width.

00:24.406 --> 00:26.440
Four times three is twelve.

00:26.890 --> 00:32.741
Area is the space inside a shape. It is not the distance around the edge.
